WEBVTT

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.417
Some people hold the view that current

00:00:03.417 --> 00:00:05.263
government policies, such as rent

00:00:05.263 --> 00:00:07.271
subsidies or preferential mortgages,

00:00:07.271 --> 00:00:09.388
seem to imply that the overall housing

00:00:09.388 --> 00:00:11.560
and rental market is just the way it is

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.221
and is very difficult to change. But

00:00:14.221 --> 00:00:16.014
it's as if they're saying, "It's okay,

00:00:16.014 --> 00:00:17.714
if you don't have enough money, I'll

00:00:17.714 --> 00:00:19.506
subsidize you; if you can't afford the

00:00:19.506 --> 00:00:21.115
rent, I'll help; if the loan isn't

00:00:21.115 --> 00:00:23.002
enough, I'll raise the limit." It makes

00:00:23.002 --> 00:00:24.818
it seem like there's nothing wrong with

00:00:24.818 --> 00:00:26.544
the environment, and the problem lies

00:00:26.544 --> 00:00:28.315
with you, which can lead to a sense of

00:00:28.315 --> 00:00:30.212
powerlessness. How do you view this

00:00:30.212 --> 00:00:32.739
kind of situation?

00:00:32.739 --> 00:00:35.057
>> Well, it’s like this: as a government

00:00:35.057 --> 00:00:39.847
, we must respond to public opinion.

00:00:39.847 --> 00:00:41.531
When there is such a demand, the

00:00:41.531 --> 00:00:43.267
government carefully considers it

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:45.257
before rolling out policies to address

00:00:45.257 --> 00:00:49.022
it.

00:00:49.022 --> 00:00:51.267
>> So, when the public—especially young

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:53.570
people—believes that housing is their

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:56.519
biggest issue,

00:00:56.519 --> 00:00:58.440
>> to the point where they don't dare to

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:00.260
start a family, or even if they do,

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.232
they don't dare to have children, then

00:01:02.232 --> 00:01:03.952
if the core issue is housing, the

00:01:03.952 --> 00:01:05.924
government has no choice but to assist

00:01:05.924 --> 00:01:08.231
in resolving this problem.

00:01:08.231 --> 00:01:10.319
>> That is why, starting from President

00:01:10.319 --> 00:01:12.351
Tsai, we have built social housing,

00:01:12.351 --> 00:01:13.988
provided rent subsidies, and

00:01:13.988 --> 00:01:16.246
implemented rental management services,

00:01:16.246 --> 00:01:18.278
and I have continued these policies

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:21.161
since taking office.

00:01:21.161 --> 00:01:22.914
>> Later on, we also launched the

00:01:22.914 --> 00:01:25.177
preferential mortgage policy, which was

00:01:25.177 --> 00:01:30.238
a direct response to public demand.

00:01:30.238 --> 00:01:32.626
Furthermore, for university students,

00:01:32.626 --> 00:01:35.140
we provide dormitory subsidies; if they

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:37.654
live at home, we offer TP travel passes

00:01:37.654 --> 00:01:43.971
to ease their burden. This is how the

00:01:43.971 --> 00:01:45.736
government responds to the needs of the

00:01:45.736 --> 00:01:49.736
people.
